{"type":"assistant","uuid":"e3330e1f-be34-46b4-91a5-e46938cc0bd5","session_id":"38a4e0ab-c5b5-4abf-984f-db4164d592e4","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"e3330e1f-be34-46b4-91a5-e46938cc0bd5","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to fix a URL encoding bug in an Android project. Let me start by understanding the bug:\n\n1. The bug is about URL encoding with `%25` (which is `%` encoded)\n2. When a URL contains `%25E6%259D%25A5%25E6%25BA%2590` (double-encoded UTF-8 for Chinese characters \"来源\"), the app should decode it properly to `%E6%9D%A5%E6%BA%90` (single-encoded)\n3. Currently, it's not handling the `%` symbol properly, causing double-encoding issues\n\nLet me explore the codebase to understand the project structure and find the relevant code.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
