{"type":"user","uuid":"48d10c5a-8208-4796-8d57-846309e610ea","session_id":"38a4e0ab-c5b5-4abf-984f-db4164d592e4","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-856e2f0329d69661","is_error":false,"content":"package com.trianguloy.urlchecker.modules.list;\n\nimport android.net.Uri;\nimport android.net.UrlQuerySanitizer;\nimport android.view.View;\nimport android.widget.Button;\nimport android.widget.LinearLayout;\nimport android.widget.TextView;\n\nimport com.trianguloy.urlchecker.R;\nimport com.trianguloy.urlchecker.activities.ModulesActivity;\nimport com.trianguloy.urlchecker.dialogs.MainDialog;\nimport com.trianguloy.urlchecker.modules.AModuleConfig;\nimport com.trianguloy.urlchecker.modules.AModuleData;\nimport com.trianguloy.urlchecker.modules.AModuleDialog;\nimport com.trianguloy.urlchecker.modules.DescriptionConfig;\nimport com.trianguloy.urlchecker.url.UrlData;\nimport com.trianguloy.urlchecker.utilities.methods.AndroidUtils;\nimport com.trianguloy.urlchecker.utilities.methods.Inflater;\nimport com.trianguloy.urlchecker.utilities.methods.JavaUtils;\n\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n/**\n * This module shows all parts of the url decoded\n */\npublic class UriPartsModule extends AModuleData {\n\n    @Override\n    public String getId() {\n        return \"uriparts\";\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public int getName() {\n        return R.string.mParts_name;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public AModuleDialog getDialog(MainDialog cntx) {\n        return new UriPartsDialog(cntx);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public AModuleConfig getConfig(ModulesActivity cntx) {\n        return new DescriptionConfig(R.string.mParts_desc);\n    }\n}\n\nclass UriPartsDialog extends AModuleDialog {\n\n    private LinearLayout box;\n    private final List<String> expandedGroups = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    public UriPartsDialog(MainDialog dialog) {\n        super(dialog);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public int getLayoutId() {\n        return R.layout.dialog_parts;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void onInitialize(View views) {\n        box = views.findViewById(R.id.box);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void onDisplayUrl(UrlData urlData) {\n        // clear\n        box.removeAllViews();\n\n        // parse\n        var uri = Uri.parse(urlData.url);\n        var urlQuerySanitizer = new UrlQuerySanitizer();\n        // the default parseUrl doesn't remove the fragment\n        if (uri.getQuery() != null) {\n            urlQuerySanitizer.setAllowUnregisteredParamaters(true);\n            urlQuerySanitizer.setUnregisteredParameterValueSanitizer(v -> v);\n            urlQuerySanitizer.parseQuery(uri.getQuery());\n        }\n\n        // domain elements\n        if (uri.getAuthority() != null || uri.getScheme() != null) {\n            var domain = addGroup(\"Domain\", -1, null);\n            addPart(\"scheme\", uri.getScheme(), domain, null);\n            addPart(\"user info\", uri.getUserInfo(), domain, null);\n            addPart(\"host\", uri.getHost(), domain, null);\n            addPart(\"port\", uri.getPort() != -1 ? String.valueOf(uri.getPort()) : null, domain, null);\n        }\n\n        // paths\n        var pathSegments = uri.getPathSegments();\n        if (pathSegments.size() > 0) {\n            var paths = addGroup(\"Paths\", pathSegments.size(), uri.buildUpon().path(null));\n            for (var i = 0; i < pathSegments.size(); i++) {\n                var pathSegment = pathSegments.get(i);\n\n                var builder = uri.buildUpon();\n                builder.path(null);\n                for (int newI = 0; newI < pathSegments.size(); newI++) {\n                    if (newI != i) builder.appendPath(pathSegments.get(newI));\n                }\n                addPart(\"/\", pathSegment, paths, builder);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // query parameters\n        var parameters = urlQuerySanitizer.getParameterList();\n        if (parameters.size() > 0) {\n            // build the delete URL query string by manually encoding params to avoid\n            // double-encoding caused by UrlQuerySanitizer (decodes) + appendQueryParameter (re-encodes) mismatch\n            String buildQuery(List<?> params, int skipIndex) {\n                var parts = new java.util.ArrayList<String>();\n                for (var j = 0; j < params.size(); j++) {\n                    if (j == skipIndex) continue;\n                    var p = params.get(j);\n                    var encoded = Uri.encode((String) p.mParameter, Uri.CODESET) + \"=\";\n                    if (p.mValue != null) {\n                        encoded += Uri.encode((String) p.mValue, Uri.CODESET);\n                    }\n                    parts.add(encoded);\n                }\n                return String.join(\"&\", parts);\n            }\n\n            var queries = addGroup(\"Parameters\", parameters.size(), uri.buildUpon().query(buildQuery(parameters, -1)));\n            for (var i = 0; i < parameters.size(); i++) {\n                // generate same url but without this parameter\n                var builder = uri.buildUpon().query(buildQuery(parameters, i));\n                // append the parameter\n                addPart(parameters.get(i).mParameter, parameters.get(i).mValue, queries, builder);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // fragment\n        if (uri.getFragment() != null) {\n            var fragment = addGroup(\"Fragment\", -1, uri.buildUpon().fragment(null));\n            addPart(\"#\", uri.getFragment(), fragment, null);\n        }\n\n        setVisibility(box.getChildCount() > 0);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Adds a collapsible group\n     */\n    private LinearLayout addGroup(String name, int size, Uri.Builder onDelete) {\n        var title = Inflater.inflate(R.layout.uri_part, box);\n        title.findViewById(R.id.key).setVisibility(View.GONE);\n\n        var name_view = title.<TextView>findViewById(R.id.value);\n        name_view.setText(name + (size <= -1 ? \"\" : \" (\" + size + \")\"));\n        AndroidUtils.setAsClickable(name_view);\n\n        var delete_view = title.<Button>findViewById(R.id.delete);\n        if (onDelete == null) delete_view.setVisibility(View.GONE);\n        else delete_view.setOnClickListener(v -> setUrl(onDelete.build().toString()));\n\n        var group = Inflater.<LinearLayout>inflate(R.layout.dialog_parts, box);\n        group.setVisibility(expandedGroups.contains(name) ? View.VISIBLE : View.GONE);\n        AndroidUtils.toggleableListener(\n                title,\n                v -> JavaUtils.toggleContains(expandedGroups, name),\n                v -> {\n                    group.setVisibility(expandedGroups.contains(name) ? View.VISIBLE : View.GONE);\n                    name_view.setCompoundDrawablesRelativeWithIntrinsicBounds(expandedGroups.contains(name) ? R.drawable.arrow_down : R.drawable.arrow_right, 0, 0, 0);\n                }\n        );\n\n        return group;\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Adds a part\n     */\n    private void addPart(String name, String value, LinearLayout container, Uri.Builder onDelete) {\n        if (value == null) return;\n        // create row\n        var part = Inflater.inflate(R.layout.uri_part, container);\n\n        // configure key\n        var key_view = part.<TextView>findViewById(R.id.key);\n        key_view.setText(name.isEmpty() ? getActivity().getString(R.string.mParts_empty) : name);\n        if (!name.isEmpty()) key_view.setOnLongClickListener(longTapToCopy);\n\n        // configure value\n        var value_view = part.<TextView>findViewById(R.id.value);\n        value_view.setText(value);\n        AndroidUtils.setAsClickable(value_view);\n        value_view.setOnClickListener(v -> setUrl(value));\n        value_view.setOnLongClickListener(longTapToCopy);\n\n        // configure delete\n        var delete_view = part.<Button>findViewById(R.id.delete);\n        if (onDelete != null) {\n            try {\n                var newUrl = onDelete.build().toString();\n                delete_view.setOnClickListener(v -> setUrl(newUrl));\n            } catch (UnsupportedOperationException ignored) {\n                delete_view.setVisibility(View.GONE);\n            }\n        } else {\n            delete_view.setVisibility(View.GONE);\n        }\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * OnLongClickListener to copy a part (textview text) to the clipboard\n     */\n    private final View.OnLongClickListener longTapToCopy = v -> {\n        AndroidUtils.copyToClipboard(getActivity(), R.string.mParts_copy, ((TextView) v).getText().toString());\n        return true;\n    };\n\n}\n"}]}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"6b228a72-740d-41c2-82ab-76e5df5c6aae","session_id":"38a4e0ab-c5b5-4abf-984f-db4164d592e4","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"6b228a72-740d-41c2-82ab-76e5df5c6aae","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The code looks correct. Let me verify:1. `buildQuery` is a local function defined inside `onDisplayUrl` that:\n   - Takes a `List<?>` of parameters and an index to skip\n   - Iterates through parameters, skipping the one at `skipIndex`\n   - For each parameter, encodes the name and value with `Uri.encode(..., Uri.CODESET)`\n   - Joins them with `&`2. `uri.buildUpon().query(buildQuery(parameters, -1))` - builds the full URL with all parameters for the group's delete button3. `uri.buildUpon().query(buildQuery(parameters, i))` - builds the URL without parameter `i` for that parameter's delete button\n\n\nLet me verify the encoding logic works correctly. When `UrlQuerySanitizer` decodes `prefill_%25E6%259D%25A5` to `prefill_来源` and `%E5%B8%AE%E5%8A%A9%E4%B8%8E%E5%8F%8D%E9%A6%88` to `帮助与反馈`, `Uri.encode` should properly re-encode them back to their percent-encoded forms. The key question is whether `Uri.CODESET` is the right constant to use here.\n\nLooking at the Android source, `Uri.CODESET` is defined as `UTF-8` for API levels 24 and above. For this project targeting API 33, that's exactly what will be used. The `Uri.encode` method applies `URLEncoder.encode` with this charset, which handles the re-encoding correctly for both ASCII and non-ASCII characters like the Chinese text in this case.\n\nI should double-check the existing code to see if `Uri.CODESET` is already being used elsewhere for consistency, and confirm that `UrlQuerySanitizer.ParameterList` has the necessary `mParameter` and `mValue` fields available.\n\nBoth fields are public instance variables in the inner class, so the implementation should work as expected.\n\nNow I'm verifying the logic handles edge cases correctly. When skipping all parameters, the parts list ends up empty and `String.join(\"&\", parts)` returns an empty string. The query parameter with just `&` as a separator also works as expected.\n\nBut there's an issue: when there are no parameters, the `Uri.Builder.query(\"\")` might not properly clear the query component depending on the Android implementation. Looking at how the original code handles this with `builder.query(null)` versus our approach with `builder.query(\"\")`, there's a discrepancy that needs addressing.\n\nI should fix this by checking if the query string is empty before setting it—if it is, use `query(null)` to clear it, otherwise use `query(query)` to set the encoded query. This ensures consistent behavior for the delete button when removing all parameters.\n\nNow I'm writing the method that builds the query string by iterating through parameters, skipping the one at the skip index, and encoding both keys and values before joining them with ampersands.\n\nI notice the `UrlQuerySanitizer.ParameterList` type might be causing issues with the generic list type, so I should verify how the parameter list is being accessed in the original code to ensure the field references are correct. I see the original code accesses `mParameter` and `mValue` directly without casting, so `var` infers the specific type from `getParameterList()`. Since that method returns a raw `List` in the Android framework, using `List<UrlQuerySanitizer.ParameterList>` would be clearer than `List<?>` with explicit casts. I'll update the lambda parameter to use the proper type instead of the generic wildcard.\n\nFor the `p.mValue` field, I should keep the null check as a defensive measure even though the sanitizer's value sanitizer always returns a non-null value—the check itself is harmless and handles edge cases safely.\n\nThe `UrlQuerySanitizer.ParameterList` class is an inner class within `UrlQuerySanitizer` that has two public String fields: `mParameter` for the key and `mValue` for the value, both accessible from the outer class. I'm confident the fix works by manually constructing the query string with proper encoding instead of relying on `appendQueryParameter` to avoid the double-encoding issue. Since I can't build the project in this environment, I'll prepare the patch output with the diff showing the changes from the original file to the fixed version.\n\nLooking back at the original code, the nested loop iterates through parameters and appends query parameters using `builder.appendQueryParameter()`, which was causing the double-encoding problem by treating the already-decoded parameter values as plain text and re-encoding them.\n\nThe core issue is that `UrlQuerySanitizer` decodes values during parsing, but then `appendQueryParameter` encodes them again on the way out—so `来源` gets re-encoded to `%E6%9D%A5%E6%BA%90` instead of preserving the original encoding. My approach bypasses this by manually handling the encoding once. I'm also considering whether `UrlQuerySanitizer` might already encode values with `%` characters (like `来源` becoming `%E6%9D%A5`), which would complicate re-encoding, but the fix handles this by constructing the query string directly without the intermediate decoding/encoding step. The issue is that `Uri.encode()` always percent-encodes `%` characters, so if the sanitizer returns an already-encoded value like `%E6%9D%A5`, it gets double-encoded to `%25E6%259D%25A5`. The expected URL should preserve the original single-encoded format, but my approach of always re-encoding breaks this. I need to detect whether the value is already encoded and handle it accordingly.\n\nLooking back at the bug report, the expected URL shows single-encoded Chinese characters, which suggests the app should perform a single URL decode on the double-encoded input. The user confirms this is about improper handling of the `%` symbol itself in URLs.\n\nThe real issue is that after parsing and displaying, the delete button