code once (via `Uri.encode`). This produces the correct single-encoded URL.\n\nThe expected URL `prefill_%E6%9D%A5%E6%BA%90` is exactly what `Uri.encode(\"来源\", \"UTF-8\")` would produce, so this approach is right. Now I'm checking the `Uri.CODESET` constant used in the Android API.\n\nIn the compiled AAR, `Uri.CODESET` is a static final String set to \"UTF-8\", which works identically to passing the string literal directly. I'm ready to finalize the patch, though I'm noticing the `null` handling in my `buildQuery` method needs review when all parameters are being removed.\n\nWhen `skipIndex` matches the only parameter, `parts` ends up empty and `String.join(\"&\", parts)` returns an empty string, so `builder.query(\"\")` clears the query as expected. But I should verify whether `Uri.Builder` handles an empty string the same way as `null`—there might be a subtle difference in behavior between these two cases. So the empty string case works fine with `appendQuery(\"\")` since `?` gets appended and then overwritten by any subsequent queries. The edge cases all check out—null clears, empty string works, and non-empty values function as expected. Now I'm verifying that my fix produces the correct output by tracing","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
