&\");\n        var p = parameters.get(j);\n        fullQuery.append(Uri.encode((String) p.mParameter, Uri.CODESET));\n        fullQuery.append(\"=\");\n        if (p.mValue != null) {\n            fullQuery.append(Uri.encode((String) p.mValue, Uri.CODESET));\n        }\n    }\n    var queries = addGroup(\"Parameters\", parameters.size(), uri.buildUpon().query(fullQuery.toString()));\n    \n    // build query strings for each \"delete this parameter\" button\n    var paramBuilders = new Uri[parameters.size()];\n    for (var i = 0; i < parameters.size(); i++) {\n        StringBuilder partQuery = new StringBuilder();\n        for (var j = 0; j < parameters.size(); j++) {\n            if (j == i) continue;\n            if (partQuery.length() > 0) partQuery.append(\"&\");\n            var p = parameters.get(j);\n            partQuery.append(Uri.encode((String) p.mParameter, Uri.CODESET));\n            partQuery.append(\"=\");\n            if (p.mValue != null) {\n                partQuery.append(Uri.encode((String) p.mValue, Uri.CODESET));\n            }\n        }\n        paramBuilders[i] = uri.buildUpon().query(partQuery.toString());\n        addPart(parameters.get(i).mParameter, parameters.get(i).mValue, queries, paramBuilders[i]);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis approach builds the full query string once for the \"delete all\" button, then iterates through each parameter to create individual query strings for the \"delete this parameter\" buttons, encoding both keys and values as needed. I see the issue with `Uri.Builder.query(\"\")` — it sets the query to an empty string rather than clearing it like `query(null)` does. The `query()` method only updates the query if the input isn't null or empty, so I need to use `query(null)` when the constructed query is empty to properly reset it.\n\nI'm refactoring the approach to build the full query string first, then create individual delete URLs for each parameter by removing one at a time from the full query.\n\nBuilding the delete 